**Drawing required (no figure supplied):** draw one long tubule with its blood supply and label, in order:

- **afferent arteriole** (wide, bringing blood in) and **efferent arteriole** (narrower, leaving), forming the **glomerulus** (knot of capillaries);
- **Bowman's capsule** (cup-shaped, surrounding the glomerulus); glomerulus and capsule together make the **Malpighian body (renal corpuscle)** in the **cortex**;
- **proximal convoluted tubule** (cortex);
- **loop of Henle** with **descending limb** and **ascending limb** (dipping into the **medulla**);
- **distal convoluted tubule** (cortex);
- **collecting duct** (running through the medulla to the pelvis);
- **peritubular capillary network** around the tubules, leading to the **renal vein branch**.

Indicate the direction of flow of blood and filtrate with arrows, and give a title.
